# Line endings.
#
# Everything in this repo is text and everything that reads it is happy with LF: the
# WoW client does not care, luacheck does not care, and CI runs lua5.1 on Linux. The
# index has been 100% LF since the repo was created, so this file changes no history --
# it only stops the working tree drifting away from it.
#
# Without this, Git for Windows' default core.autocrlf=true converts LF to CRLF on
# checkout, so files Git writes are CRLF while files an editor or a tool writes are LF.
# That split is what produces "LF will be replaced by CRLF the next time Git touches it"
# on every `git add`. Committing this is the fix; `git config core.safecrlf false` only
# silences the report.
#
# eol=lf rather than eol=native deliberately: native would reintroduce exactly the CRLF
# conversion above on Windows.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary formats a WoW addon might grow. `text=auto` usually detects these correctly,
# but .blp and .tga are obscure enough to be worth stating rather than trusting.
*.blp binary
*.tga binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ttf binary
*.ogg binary
*.mp3 binary
